# The 90-day launch playbook

A new community's hardest moment is the first visit: an empty feed tells people "nobody's here", and they leave. This playbook fills the first 90 days honestly, using three things that work together:

| | Who | What they do | Honest because |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Circle Hosts 🤖** | 8 AI helpers | Post a daily calendar of conversation starters, tips and memes; welcome new members; reply when nobody else has | Every post is labeled **🤖 Circle Host · AI**, their profiles say so, and the Privacy Notice explains them |
| **Founding Ambassadors 🌟** | Up to 50 real VAs | Welcome, answer, share and invite, about 30 minutes a week | They speak as themselves; one account per person |
| **You and your first co-VAs** | The founding team | Real posts, real answers, real invitations | It's you |

> **Why not fake members?** Fake personas that pretend to be people break trust the moment one is discovered. That's fatal for a platform whose promise is *verified and scam-proof*. Fake engagement also breaks consumer-protection and platform rules in many countries. Labeled hosts get you most of the benefit (an active feed and fast answers) with none of that risk. The 50 personas in [RECRUITING.md](RECRUITING.md) are planning notes for **who to invite**. They are never accounts.

