## 1. Circle Hosts (labeled AI)

| Host | Role | Posts |
|---|---|---|
| 🌙 **Luna** | Night-shift host, welcomes | Morning check-in questions (odd days), private welcome notifications, gentle replies to unanswered *struggles* (resources only, never advice) |
| ✨ **Glow** | Celebrations | Win and milestone prompts (even days), cheers for unanswered *wins* |
| 🎓 **Coach Sage** | Circle Academy | Daily skill tip, first reply to unanswered *questions* |
| 🔎 **Shield** | Circle Scam-Buster | Weekly scam-awareness tip (Wednesdays) |
| 😂 **Punchline** | Circle Laughs | Nightly meme, Monday "finish this sentence" prompt |
| 🌏 **Aurora** · 🌊 **Coral** · 🌄 **Summit** | Hub hosts (north · central · south) | Evening conversation starters in the regional hubs |

**Daily rhythm (Manila time):** 7:30 feed question or win prompt · 9:00 Monday Laughs prompt · 12:00 tip · 18:00 hub question · 21:00 meme.
The hosts only wake up when someone visits the site (at most every 10 minutes), so on a quiet day a post that would go out more than 2½ hours late is skipped instead of appearing out of time (`hosts_late_minutes`, default 150). The Monday prompt may still go out later that day, and if the team already set a prompt that week, Punchline keeps yours.
The 90 days follow a weekly theme: welcome → night-shift survival → first clients → tools → client communication → rates and getting paid → scam awareness → boundaries and burnout → upskilling → home life → newbie to seasoned → giving back → celebrating 90 days.

**What hosts never do:** DM anyone, connect, join Circle BFF, apply for jobs, appear in Talent, Squads, podcast credits or the Hall of Fame, review, pay or get paid (their referral codes earn nothing), take a Founders Cohort slot, count as members, or log in. The 🤖 label comes from the account itself, and members can't register names containing "Circle Host" or "(AI)", so nobody can pass as a host. They never claim to be human, invent testimonials or statistics, or give medical, legal or tax certainty.

**They step back on their own.** The hosts check how many posts *real* members made per day over the last week (`hosts_fade_posts_per_day`, default 25):
- below 25/day: normal calendar
- 25–49/day: **light mode**, only the daily tip and Monday prompt
- 50+/day: **calendar paused**; welcomes and replies to unanswered posts continue (those still help)

**Your controls (Circle Ops → Hosts):** switch on/off · set Day 1 · see today's day of 90 and the fade level · preview the next 7 days, memes included · **Edit**, **Skip** or **Un-skip** any upcoming post · **Run now** (only while switched on) · activity log. The Founder, GM and IT admin control the switch, Day 1 and Run now; other staff can edit and skip.
Settings in Circle Ops → Settings: `hosts_reply_after_hours` (default 3), `hosts_fade_posts_per_day` (default 25), `hosts_late_minutes` (default 150).
With a `GEMINI_API_KEY`, replies to questions are written by AI under strict rules (labeled, no links, no certainty, invites real VAs to add their experience). If an AI reply ever contains a link, handle or contact detail, it is thrown away and the built-in reply is used instead. Without a key, built-in replies point to the right Circle feature.

**Before Day 1:** the hosts stay completely quiet after you deploy until you choose Day 1, so there's time to read the first week in Circle Ops → Hosts and skip or edit anything that doesn't sound like your circle. To rewrite the calendar in bulk, edit a JSON copy and run `node dev/build-host-calendar.mjs calendar.json` (it rejects contact details and links and flags anything that sounds human, non-English or brand-based), then redeploy: posts that haven't gone out yet pick up the new wording automatically, and posts your team edited in Circle Ops keep your edits.

